00:31:14.639 --> 00:31:16.808
Orange mango, fruit punch, lemonade.

00:31:16.808 --> 00:31:18.810
The cherry is clear.

00:31:18.810 --> 00:31:20.678
What? Why is cherry clear?

00:31:20.678 --> 00:31:22.447
Guava splash, orange mango.

00:31:22.447 --> 00:31:23.781
♪ These are bad ♪

00:31:23.781 --> 00:31:26.050
7-Eleven energy.

00:31:26.050 --> 00:31:27.619
"Strawberry lemonade energy shot,

00:31:27.619 --> 00:31:29.821
one and half times the
caffeine of a cup of coffee."

00:31:29.821 --> 00:31:31.089
Oh, good God.

00:31:34.492 --> 00:31:35.393
Undrinkable.

00:31:35.393 --> 00:31:37.195
How bad does it have to
taste where this is too --

00:31:37.195 --> 00:31:38.029
I couldn't get to this?

00:31:38.029 --> 00:31:39.163
You've seen this show, right?

00:31:39.163 --> 00:31:40.732
You'll see what I'll tolerate.

00:31:40.732 --> 00:31:42.300
This, I can barely tolerate this.

00:31:45.136 --> 00:31:48.640
Here's something that
they don't have in Japan.

00:31:48.640 --> 00:31:49.641
They don't have Slurpees.

00:31:49.641 --> 00:31:50.842
That's nuts, right?

00:31:50.842 --> 00:31:52.710
Slurpees are -- how do
you describe a Slurpee?

00:31:52.710 --> 00:31:55.446
It's like a flavored slush.

00:31:55.446 --> 00:31:57.315
We have endless Slurpee flavors.

00:31:57.315 --> 00:31:59.884
The ones currently you can
get here in America are

00:31:59.884 --> 00:32:01.386
blue rocketberry,

00:32:01.386 --> 00:32:02.353
blood orange,

00:32:02.353 --> 00:32:03.988
Vitaminwater XXX,

00:32:03.988 --> 00:32:05.089
blue raspberry,

00:32:05.089 --> 00:32:06.858
blueberry lemonade bliss,

00:32:06.858 --> 00:32:08.459
cherry, Coca-Cola,

00:32:08.459 --> 00:32:10.695
Mountain Dew citrus, peach perfect,

00:32:10.695 --> 00:32:14.198
piña colada, and pineapple whip.

00:32:14.198 --> 00:32:16.601
So, here are Japanese exclusive drinks.

00:32:16.601 --> 00:32:19.237
We have vegetable juice, of course.

00:32:20.138 --> 00:32:22.507
Mm! Oishii.

00:32:22.507 --> 00:32:25.910
A lot of Japanese salarymen
drink this one every morning

00:32:25.910 --> 00:32:28.246
to get their day started.

00:32:28.246 --> 00:32:30.481
So this one is for Joe.

00:32:30.481 --> 00:32:33.151
Joe, you're missing a lot of veggies,

00:32:33.151 --> 00:32:35.253
so you should drink this one.

00:32:35.253 --> 00:32:38.957
Oi Ocha, my favorite green tea.

00:32:38.957 --> 00:32:41.392
And these two are hot drinks,

00:32:41.392 --> 00:32:44.195
black coffee and café latte.

00:32:44.195 --> 00:32:46.864
And this is our first time filming this.

00:32:46.864 --> 00:32:48.666
We have alcohol.

00:32:48.666 --> 00:32:51.970
We have 7-Premium beer.

00:32:51.970 --> 00:32:53.671
And this one is not beer.

00:32:53.671 --> 00:32:56.541
It's like Sprite with alcohol.

00:32:56.541 --> 00:32:59.477
It contains 9% of alcohol.

00:32:59.477 --> 00:33:00.979
It's pretty delicious,

00:33:00.979 --> 00:33:03.247
but at the same time,
it's pretty dangerous.

00:33:03.247 --> 00:33:05.350
Japanese sake.

00:33:05.350 --> 00:33:07.118
When you come to Japan, you can see

00:33:07.118 --> 00:33:09.921
a lot of people drinking alcohol outside.

00:33:09.921 --> 00:33:12.623
They're like [groans].

00:33:14.492 --> 00:33:16.894
They are not dead, they're just sleeping.

00:33:16.894 --> 00:33:18.162
They're drunk.

00:33:18.162 --> 00:33:19.197
Whisky.

00:33:19.197 --> 00:33:22.400
7-Eleven in the US has its own

00:33:22.400 --> 00:33:24.669
private brand wines,

00:33:24.669 --> 00:33:27.538
Yosemite Road, Trojan Horse,

00:33:27.538 --> 00:33:30.508
Plot and Point, and Voyager Point.

00:33:30.508 --> 00:33:33.978
It also has its own canned
wine brand, called Roamer.

00:33:33.978 --> 00:33:37.148
Perhaps the reason 7-Eleven
has such a wide variety

00:33:37.148 --> 00:33:40.985
of products in Japan is that
it's everywhere in Japan.

00:33:40.985 --> 00:33:44.956
There are 21,215 stores in Japan.

00:33:44.956 --> 00:33:46.491
That's crazy!

00:33:46.491 --> 00:33:50.595
Which is nearly 30% of all
the 7-Elevens in the world.

00:33:50.595 --> 00:33:54.265
Of course, all 37
prefectures have a 7-Eleven.

00:33:54.265 --> 00:33:55.967
And out of all of them,

00:33:55.967 --> 00:33:58.503
the city of Tokyo has the most locations,

00:33:58.503 --> 00:34:00.972
with 2,850.

00:34:00.972 --> 00:34:02.073
To put that in perspective,

00:34:02.073 --> 00:34:05.476
the US has 9,417 7-Elevens,

00:34:05.476 --> 00:34:08.179
and there's no 7-Elevens in 18 states.

00:34:08.179 --> 00:34:10.615
As far as states, California has the most,

00:34:10.615 --> 00:34:13.217
1,823.

00:34:13.217 --> 00:34:16.754
But as far as denseness in area,

00:34:16.754 --> 00:34:20.992
Las Vegas, Nevada, has the most, with 158.

00:34:23.194 --> 00:34:26.631
In Japan, our hot dog is 290 calories

00:34:26.631 --> 00:34:29.200
and 720 milligrams of sodium,

00:34:29.200 --> 00:34:33.471
which is 31.3% of your daily allowance.

00:34:33.471 --> 00:34:35.039
Our hot dog is 180 calories.

00:34:35.039 --> 00:34:36.707
Ooh. How about this?

00:34:36.707 --> 00:34:39.544
Our hot dog is 180 calories,
but for the frank only.

00:34:39.544 --> 00:34:40.812
The stats, for some reason,

00:34:40.812 --> 00:34:42.346
don't say anything about the bun.

00:34:42.346 --> 00:34:44.382
But this isn't much better for you.

00:34:44.382 --> 00:34:46.851
It's 570 milligrams of sodium,

00:34:46.851 --> 00:34:50.488
so around 24.8% of your daily allowance.

00:34:50.488 --> 00:34:53.091
Japan's hand-rolled tuna and mayo onigiri

00:34:53.091 --> 00:34:56.961
has 258 calories and is very filling.

00:34:56.961 --> 00:34:58.896
Remember this guy? The tuna sandwich.

00:34:58.896 --> 00:35:01.999
Here in the US, ours is 420 calories

00:35:01.999 --> 00:35:05.303
and lots of sodium, over 800 milligrams.

00:35:05.303 --> 00:35:06.471
Fuck!

00:35:06.471 --> 00:35:09.373
And in the US, a Super
Big Gulp of Coca-Cola,

00:35:09.373 --> 00:35:12.376
this isn't Coca-Cola, is 44 fluid ounces.

00:35:12.376 --> 00:35:16.581
It's 513 calories and 143 grams of carbs.

00:35:16.581 --> 00:35:19.016
That's over half your daily intake.

00:35:20.918 --> 00:35:23.554
In Japan, 7-Eleven does not disclose

00:35:23.554 --> 00:35:27.058
the ingredients list of its
freshly made food items.

00:35:27.058 --> 00:35:29.994
It does, however, tell
us the country of origin

00:35:29.994 --> 00:35:32.363
for the raw materials for certain items,

00:35:32.363 --> 00:35:35.366
like the fried food, yakitori, oden,

00:35:35.366 --> 00:35:37.368
and Chinese steamed buns.

00:35:37.368 --> 00:35:40.171
The chicken for our fried
chicken is from Thailand.

00:35:40.171 --> 00:35:42.673
The pork for our sausages and hot dogs

00:35:42.673 --> 00:35:45.776
comes from USA, Canada, and Japan.

00:35:45.776 --> 00:35:48.112
The wheat for the buns comes from Canada,

00:35:48.112 --> 00:35:50.114
the USA, and Japan.

00:35:50.114 --> 00:35:52.450
And adzuki beans come from Canada,

00:35:52.450 --> 00:35:54.352
cheese comes from New Zealand,

00:35:54.352 --> 00:35:57.822
and the shrimp for the shrimp
chili buns is from Vietnam.

00:35:57.822 --> 00:35:59.657
This is the pepperoni pizza in the US.

00:35:59.657 --> 00:36:02.593
And it contains all this junk.

00:36:02.593 --> 00:36:05.696
I mean, what's this thing?

00:36:05.696 --> 00:36:07.965
Never heard of that.

00:36:07.965 --> 00:36:09.467
What about chicken strips?

00:36:09.467 --> 00:36:11.235
It's got all this stuff!

00:36:11.235 --> 00:36:12.904
Just like mom used to make.

00:36:12.904 --> 00:36:15.773
And, of course, the 7-Eleven
Select cheeseburger,

00:36:15.773 --> 00:36:17.642
which contains ... [sighs]

00:36:17.642 --> 00:36:19.744
sesame seed bun has enriched flour,

00:36:19.744 --> 00:36:21.212
